## 3. Typography

### 3.1 Type Scale

**Primary Typeface:** `Inter` (Google Fonts — weights: 400, 500, 600, 700)
- Rationale: Highest legibility at all sizes; the de-facto standard for professional SaaS; pairs well with the precision aesthetic.

**Accent Typeface:** `Playfair Display` (Google Fonts — weights: 400, 700)
- Used exclusively for: certificate candidate name, hero headline on landing page, section-level "pull quotes."
- Rationale: Introduces editorial prestige without going decorative.

**Monospace:** `JetBrains Mono` (Google Fonts — weights: 400, 600)
- Used for: certificate ID display, question IDs, domain labels, timer numbers.
- Rationale: Technical precision signal; extremely legible for countdown numbers.

```css
/* Type Scale — using fluid clamp() sizing */
--text-xs:   clamp(0.688rem, 0.65rem + 0.18vw, 0.75rem);    /* 11–12px */
--text-sm:   clamp(0.813rem, 0.78rem + 0.18vw, 0.875rem);   /* 13–14px */
--text-base: clamp(0.938rem, 0.9rem + 0.2vw, 1rem);         /* 15–16px */
--text-lg:   clamp(1.063rem, 1rem + 0.3vw, 1.125rem);       /* 17–18px */
--text-xl:   clamp(1.188rem, 1.1rem + 0.4vw, 1.25rem);      /* 19–20px */
--text-2xl:  clamp(1.375rem, 1.25rem + 0.6vw, 1.5rem);      /* 22–24px */
--text-3xl:  clamp(1.75rem, 1.5rem + 1.2vw, 2rem);          /* 28–32px */
--text-4xl:  clamp(2.25rem, 1.8rem + 2vw, 2.75rem);         /* 36–44px */
--text-5xl:  clamp(2.75rem, 2rem + 3vw, 3.75rem);           /* 44–60px */
--text-hero: clamp(3.25rem, 2.5rem + 4vw, 5rem);            /* 52–80px */
